{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final plan-review attempt BLOCKED; leaving open per operator instruction. Verbatim blocking findings:\\n\\n- The 'Final plan-review amendment' asserts a sibling precedent that does not exist: 'infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e.sh is tested by tests/test_feature_branch_e2e.py.' The script exists, but tests/test_feature_branch_e2e.py is absent from the repo (read errors 'No such file'; repo-wide search for the name returns no matches). The observed script-test convention is instead tests/scripts/ (e.g. tests/scripts/test_feature_branch_inventory.py owns infra/gerrit/feature-branch-inventory.sh). Because the plan uses this precedent to justify the new test's exact path/convention (tests/test_reviewbot_e2e.py, 'same top-level tests convention as tests/test_feature_branch_e2e.py'), the chosen location rests on a false premise and diverges from the real convention.\\n\\n- The 'Final plan-review amendment' cites tests/test_feature_branch_e2e.py as an existing precedent test for infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e.sh, but that file does not exist anywhere in the repo.\\n\\n- The live PASS path can never earn Verified+1 unless the disposable rebar-ticket is resolvable in the GitHub `tickets` store that CI's ticket gate reads; the plan specifies a 'resolvable full-canonical trailer' and a 'live disposable ticket' but not that the ticket must be published to the tickets branch before CI runs.\\n\\n- The Final amendment's approach rests on a precedent that does not exist: it names `tests/test_feature_branch_e2e.py` as the sibling owner test to mirror, but there is no such file and feature-branch-e2e.sh has no Python owner test.\\n\\n- The 'Final plan-review amendment' asserts as a repository fact that infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e.sh is tested by tests/test_feature_branch_e2e.py and uses that as the precedent for the new test's path/convention, but no such test file exists in the repo."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788785738594544001,"uuid":"78e9a554-7b3c-4864-a307-32353057eb2d"}